      "original_url": "https://www.tracesofwar.com/sights/8441/Memorial-AW-Whitley-Bomber-Z6639-Broadway.htm",
      "summary": "Traces of War documents a memorial at Broadway, Worcestershire to a Whitley bomber from 24 OTU that crashed on 2 June 1943 at 14:15 hours during operational training. Five crew members were killed: Flt/Sgt H.G. Hagen (pilot), Sgt R.S. Phillips (navigator), Flt/Sgt D.H. Kelly, Sgt D.A. Marriott, and Sgt G.E. Ekins.",
      "key_details": [
        "Crash time recorded as 14:15 hours",
