        "Memorial located at Broadway, Worcestershire"
      ],
      "date_retrieved": "2026-03-23",
      "still_live": false,
      "link_description": "Poignant memorial honoring five fallen Whitley bomber crew members in Honeybourne area."
    },
    {
      "source_site": "Wartime Memories Project",
      "original_url": "https://www.wartimememoriesproject.com/ww2/airfields/airfield.php?pid=1766",
      "summary": "The Wartime Memories Project documents RAF Honeybourne as the base for No. 24 OTU during WW2. The unit used Whitley bombers for training and suffered numerous losses in the surrounding countryside, including the Z2639 incident.",
      "key_details": [
        "RAF Honeybourne documented as 24 OTU base",
        "Multiple training losses recorded in area"
      ],
